Here is an example of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code that creates a modal window with a fake chat history:
```
<!-- HTML -->
<!-- The modal window -->
<div id="myModal" class="modal">
  <!-- Modal content -->
  <div class="modal-content">
    <span class="close">&times;</span>
    <h2>Chat History</h2>
    <div class="chat-log">
      <!-- Chat messages will be rendered here -->
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Button to open the modal -->
<button id="openModal">View Chat History</button>

<!-- JavaScript -->
<script>
  // Get the modal and button elements
  var modal = document.getElementById("myModal");
  var btn = document.getElementById("openModal");
  var span = document.getElementsByClassName("close")[0];

  // Add event listeners to open and close the modal
  btn.onclick = function() {
    modal.style.display = "block";
  }
  span.onclick = function() {
    modal.style.display = "none";
  }
  window.onclick = function(event) {
    if (event.target == modal) {
      modal.style.display = "none";
    }
  }

  // Render the chat history
  var chatLog = document.querySelector(".chat-log");
  var messages = [
    { text: "Hello, how can I assist you today?", from: "AI" },
    { text: "Hi, I'm looking for information on machine learning.", from: "Human" },
    { text: "Great topic! I can provide you with some resources. Would you like me to share some articles?", from: "AI" },
    { text: "That would be amazing, thank you!", from: "Human" }
  ];

  messages.forEach(function(message) {
    var messageHTML = `<div class="chat-message ${message.from === "AI" ? "ai-message" : "human-message"}">
                        <span>${message.text}</span>
                      </div>`;
    chatLog.innerHTML += messageHTML;
  });
</script>

<!-- CSS -->
<style>
  /* The modal window */
  .modal {
    display: none; /* Hidden by default */
    position: fixed; /* Stay in place */
    z-index: 1; /* Sit on top */
    padding-top: 100px; /* Location of the box */
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 100%; /* Full width */
    height: 100%; /* Full height */
    overflow: auto; /* Enable scroll if needed */
    background-color: rgb(0,0,0); /* Fallback color */
    background-color: rgba(0,0,0,0.4); /* Black w/ opacity */
  }

  /* Modal Content */
  .modal-content {
    background-color: #fefefe;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid #888;
    width: 80%;
  }

  /* The Close Button */
  .close {
    color: #aaaaaa;
    float: right;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .close:hover,
  .close:focus {
    color: #000;
    text-decoration: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Chat log styles */
  .chat-log {
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .chat-message {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .ai-message {
    background-color: #f0f0f0;
    padding: 10px;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .human-message {
    background-color: #ccc;
    padding: 10px;
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
</style>
```
This code creates a modal window with a chat log that displays 4 messages: 2 from the AI chatbot and 2 from the human user. The chat messages are rendered dynamically using JavaScript. The CSS styles the modal window, chat log, and individual chat messages.

Note that this is just a simple example, and you may want to add more features to your fake chatbot, such as user input fields, scrolling, and animation.

